IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cards-domain`
IMPORT `earn-kernel`
IMPORT fixtures

§ `Standard Chartered Credit Cards Retail Transaction Exclusions`

-- ===========================================================================
-- DOCUMENT. sc-cc-retail-exclusions: the "Standard Chartered Credit Cards
-- Retail Transaction Exclusions" page on sc.com/sg (Standard Chartered Bank
-- (Singapore) Limited), held by clause-text digest. It carries no version or
-- date; the MCC table marks some rows "*Effective 3 September 2024".
-- INCORPORATED BY REFERENCE by the Smart Credit Card Promotion T&C ("Selected
-- transactions set out in Standard Chartered Credit Card Retail Transaction
-- Exclusions will not be considered as Eligible Retail Transactions and are
-- not eligible to earn any 360° Rewards Points").
--
-- WHAT THE PAGE SAYS: "The following transactions are not Eligible Retail
-- Transactions and will not earn Cashback or 360° Rewards Points:" and then
-- fifteen classes: cash advance; Credit Card Funds Transfer; monthly
-- instalment of an EasyPay transaction; amounts subsequently cancelled,
-- voided, refunded or reversed; AXS, SAM or ATM transactions; insurance
-- premiums; recurring payments ("automatic payments where the Cardholder ...
-- has given a one-time authorisation or instruction for the merchant to charge
-- the payment directly to his/her Card at a fixed interval") or "payments made
-- to all billing organisations using Standard Chartered Online Banking or
-- mobile app"; fees or charges; amounts rolled over from a preceding
-- statement; tax refunds credited to the Card; charges not submitted or posted
-- in the period; fraudulent transactions; betting; top-ups or payment of funds
-- to prepaid cards and accounts "including without limitation" a list of
-- named accounts; and any transaction under thirty-five listed MCCs.
--
-- THE FORK F-sc-simplygo. The named-accounts list ends "... SIMPLYGO ...
-- TRANSITLINK*". The Smart promotion terms name "BUS/MRT via SimplyGo" as a
-- Bonus Merchant. Reading 1: the SIMPLYGO entry sits in a sentence about
-- "top-ups or payment of funds to the following accounts", so it excludes
-- SimplyGo TOP-UPS and not the bus and train fares that are the Bonus Merchant.
-- Reading 2: it excludes every transaction bearing the SIMPLYGO description,
-- fares included, which would leave the Bonus Merchant empty. The module takes
-- Reading 1 as the answer and reports Reading 2 as an open condition on a fare
-- whose statement line bears the SimplyGo description. ASSUMED, NOT RULED.
--
-- BILL PAYMENTS. The page excludes "payments made to all billing organisations
-- using Standard Chartered Online Banking or mobile app", not every bill: a
-- bill paid directly to the biller on the card is not within that sentence, and
-- is within the recurring-payment sentence only if it is a standing instruction.
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `The charge kinds the page names`

GIVEN k IS A `Charge kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the SC page excludes the kind` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `Retail purchase`                                   THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Bill payment`                                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Bill paid directly to the biller on the card`      THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Top-up of a prepaid card or stored-value account`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Payment of funds to a payment service provider`    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Instalment plan charge`                            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `My Preferred Payment Plan charge`                  THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Cash advance`                                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Balance transfer or funds transfer`                THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Fee, interest or finance charge`                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Pre-authorisation`                                 THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Payment through UOB Payment Facility`              THEN FALSE
    WHEN `NETS or NETS-related transaction`                  THEN FALSE
    WHEN `SmartPay or personal loan`                         THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Transit-related transaction`                       THEN FALSE

-- "recurring payments": the presentation is a standing instruction.
GIVEN how IS A Presentation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the SC page excludes the presentation` how MEANS
    how EQUALS `Recurring payment arrangement`


§§ `The Merchant Category Codes the page lists`

-- 4829, 4900*, 5047*, 5199*, 6012, 6050*, 6051, 6540, 6211, 6513, 6529*, 6530*,
-- 6534*, 7299*, 7349, 7511*, 7523, 8062*, 8211, 8220, 8241, 8244, 8249, 8299,
-- 8398, 8651, 8661, 8999*, 9211, 9222, 9223, 9311, 9399, 9402, 9405.
-- (* effective 3 September 2024.)
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the SC excluded category codes` MEANS
    LIST 4829, 4900, 5047, 5199, 6012, 6050, 6051, 6540, 6211, 6513, 6529, 6530,
         6534, 7299, 7349, 7511, 7523, 8062, 8211, 8220, 8241, 8244, 8249, 8299,
         8398, 8651, 8661, 8999, 9211, 9222, 9223, 9311, 9399, 9402, 9405

GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the SC page lists the code of` p MEANS
    `the code is among` p `the SC excluded category codes`


§§ `The named accounts and descriptions`

-- The prepaid-account entries: EZ LINK (and EZ-LINK PTE LTD SINGAPORE, EZ LINK
-- PTE LTD, EZ-LINK TOP-UP KIOSK, EZ LINK PTE LTD (FEVO), EZ-LINK (IMAGINE CARD),
-- EZLINK*, EZLINKS.COM), FLASHPAY ATU, TRANSIT, TRANSIT LINK PL, TRANSIT LINK*,
-- TRANSITLINK*, PAYPAL * BIZCONSULTA, PAYPAL * CAPITALROYA. SIMPLYGO is the
-- seventeenth entry and is handled separately (fork F-sc-simplygo).
GIVEN d IS A Descriptor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the SC page names the description` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `EZ-Link`                                             THEN TRUE
    WHEN `FlashPay`                                            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `TRANSIT`                                             THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Transit Link`                                        THEN TRUE
    WHEN `PayPal Bizconsulta or Capitalroya or Oandaasiapa`    THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE                                                       FALSE

GIVEN d IS A Descriptor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the SC page names SIMPLYGO` d MEANS
    d EQUALS `SimplyGo as a descriptor`


§§ `Whether the page excludes a purchase`

GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the SC page excludes` p MEANS
    `the SC page excludes the kind` (p's `charge kind`)
    OR `the SC page excludes the presentation` (p's presentation)
    OR p's `posting status` EQUALS `Authorised but not posted`
    OR p's `later reversed`
    OR `the SC page lists the code of` p
    OR `the SC page names the description` (p's descriptor)

-- TRUE iff only Reading 2 of the SIMPLYGO entry would exclude it: the
-- statement line bears the SimplyGo description, and nothing else excludes it.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`only the SIMPLYGO entry would exclude` p MEANS
    `the SC page names SIMPLYGO` (p's descriptor)
    AND NOT (`the SC page excludes` p)


§§ `Illustrations`

#ASSERT NOT (`the SC page excludes` `the base purchase`)
#ASSERT `the SC page excludes` (`purchase of kind` `the base purchase` `Cash advance`)
#ASSERT `the SC page excludes` (`purchase of kind` `the base purchase` `Balance transfer or funds transfer`)
#ASSERT `the SC page excludes` (`purchase of kind` `the base purchase` `Instalment plan charge`)
#ASSERT `the SC page excludes` (`purchase of kind` `the base purchase` `Fee, interest or finance charge`)
#ASSERT `the SC page excludes` (`purchase of kind` `the base purchase` `Top-up of a prepaid card or stored-value account`)
#ASSERT `the SC page excludes` (`purchase of kind` `the base purchase` `Bill payment`)
#ASSERT `the SC page excludes` (`purchase paid by` `the base purchase` `Recurring payment arrangement`)
#ASSERT `the SC page excludes` (`purchase with status` `the base purchase` `Authorised but not posted`)
#ASSERT `the SC page excludes` (`purchase later reversed` `the base purchase`)

-- A bill paid directly to the biller on the card is not within the page's sentence.
#ASSERT NOT (`the SC page excludes` (`purchase of kind` `the base purchase` `Bill paid directly to the biller on the card`))

